Equip (Page: 504)

E*quip" (?), v. t. [imp. & p. p. Equipped (?); p. pr. & vb. n. Equipping.] [F. équiper to supply, fit out, orig. said of a ship, OF. esquiper to embark; of German origin; compare OHG. scif, G. schiff, Icel. skip, AS. scip. See Ship.]

